WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
A calculator cover opens QP1NG with the demo PIN.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.500
The Fallout dashboard brings communications, local tools and network status together.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.967
Prepare a message in Q-Chat. This sample contact and draft stay in the demo; nothing is sent.

4
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:15.833
Enable Ghost mode: its message database lives in RAM for the session.

5
00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:21.800
Share the demo identity through an animated QR, without a phone number.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.800
Start Bluetooth mesh and discover nearby devices. No second peer is connected in this recording.

7
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.767
Open Local Wi-Fi: messages, files and calls can use a shared Wi-Fi network or offline hotspot.

8
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:39.267
Create a private QR invitation for the other phone. Pairing is waiting; no transfer is shown.

9
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:44.233
Run the Tor check: verify the local SOCKS proxy and exit node. Waiting time is shortened.

10
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:49.233
Inspect the verified circuit and its relays on the globe.

11
00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:53.200
Choose a startup cover: calculator, weather or tile puzzle.

12
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.000
Open access protocols from Secure Settings, alongside startup and sensitive-page locks.

13
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.467
Primary, duress and decoy credentials have separate fields. This is a settings view; no wipe is performed.

14
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:04.133
One app: private identity, local connections and controls you can inspect.
